---
title: "close_and_withdraw (Sui Framework: kiosk)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_destruct: Kiosk + KioskOwnerCap destructured
    q_destruct --> q_check_owner: assert id.to_inner() == cap.for
    q_check_owner --> q_abort_owner: IDs don't match
    q_abort_owner --> [*]: abort ENotOwner
    q_check_owner --> q_check_empty: IDs match
    q_check_empty --> q_abort_empty: item_count != 0
    q_abort_empty --> [*]: abort ENotEmpty
    q_check_empty --> q_delete: item_count == 0
    q_delete --> q_delete_cap: cap_id.delete()
    q_delete_cap --> q_delete_kiosk: id.delete()
    q_delete_kiosk --> [*]: return profits.into_coin(ctx)

    note right of q_check_empty
        INV-001: kiosk must be empty to close (no stranded items)
        INV-002: both kiosk and cap are destroyed
        INV-003: all remaining profits returned as coin
    end note
